title: 'import is neither atomic nor lenient: one bad file leaves the board half-written'
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`BoardStore.pm:290-328`. One malformed file aborts the import mid-write:

    # tasks/: 3 valid files + 1 broken
    karr import --yes   -> "Invalid task format"   rc=1
    karr list --compact -> #1, #2          # #3 missing, prune never ran

The board is left half-imported with stale refs, and the error message does not
name the offending file, so the user has to guess which one it was.

kanban-md uses `ReadAllLenient` and reports `Warning: skipping malformed file
<name>: <reason>`, then carries on.

Fix: parse everything first, report every bad file by name, and only then write —
so the board is either fully updated or untouched. The same "name the file"
point applies to the CRLF rejection path (`Task.pm:141` requires `\A---\n`,
which is correct parity, but the message is a bare "Invalid task format").
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
